{
  "title": "Ziyarah on the Id al-Fitr and Id al-Azha days",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "It is worth mentioning that scholars have dedicated two forms of ziyarah to these two blessed feast days (i.e. ‘Id al-Fitr and ‘Id al-Azha). The first form has been previously cited as the ziyarah form at the Qadr Nights, while the other is the following. What is apparently understood from the words of the scholars is that the first form of ziyarah is said when one visits the holy shrine on the two days of ‘Id al-Fitr and ‘Id al-Azha, while the following form is said when the holy shrine is visited at the two nights before these two days. Thus, the ziyarah form is as follows:\nWhen you intend to visit Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)’s tomb at these two nights, you may stop at the gate of the holy dome, cast your sight on the tomb, and seek permission of admission by saying,\nیَا مَوْلَایَ یَا اَبَا عَبْدِ اﷲِ یَابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اﷲِ \nYAA MAWLAAYA YAA ABAA A’BDILLAAHE YABNA RASOOLILLAAHE\nO my master, O Abu Abdullah, O the son of the Apostle of Allah, \nعَبْدُكَ وَابْنُ اَمَتِكَ الذَّلِیْلُ بَیْنَ یَدَیْكَ \nA’BDOKA WABNO AMATEKAZ ZALEELO BAYNA YADAYKA\nYour servant and the son of your servant and your maid, degraded in front of you and \nوَالْمُصَغَّرُ فِیْ عُلُوِّ قَدْرِكَ وَالْمُعْتَرِفُ \nWAL MOSAGHGHARO FEE O’LUWWE QADREKA WAL MO’TAREFO\ndiminutive in front of your lofty stature, attestor of \nبِحَقِّكَ جَآئَكَ مُسْتَجِیْرًا بِكَ قَاصِداً اِلیٰ \nBE HAQQEKA JAAA-AKA MUSTAJEERAN BEKA QAASEDAN ELAA\nyour right, He has come to you seeking refuge in you, entrant in \nحَرَمِكَ مُتَوَجِّهًا اِلیٰ مَقَامِكَ مُتَوَسِّلًا اِلَی \nHARAMEKA MOTAWAJJEHAN ELAA MAQAAMEKA MOTAWASSELAN ELAL\nyour sanctuary, facing your position beseeching Allah \nاﷲِ تَعَالیٰ بِكَ ءَ اَدْخُلُ یَا مَوْلَایَ ءَاَدْخُلُ \nLAAHE TA-A’ALAA BEKA A-ADKHOLO YAA MAWLAAYA A-ADKHOLO \nthrough you, Do I enter, O my master. Do I enter, \nیَا وَلِیَّ اﷲِ ءَاَدْخُلُ یَا مَلَائِكَۃَ اﷲِ \nYAA WALIYYALLAAHE A-ADKHOLO YAA MALAAA-EKATALLAAHIL\nO the representative of Allah? Do I enter, O the angels of Allah \nالْمُحْدِقِیْنَ بِهٰذَا الْحَرَمِ الْمُقِیْمِیْنَ فِیْ \nMOHDEQEENA BE HAAZAL HARAMIL MOQEEMEENA FEE\nwho enrich this sanctuary, and reside in \nھٰذَا الْمَشْهَدِ\nHAAZAL MASH-HADE\nthis holy shrine?\nIf your heart feels reverence and your eyes shed tears, then you may enter by preceding your right foot to your left one. You may then say the following words:\nبِسْمِ اﷲِ وَ بِاﷲِ وَ فِیْ سَبِیْلِ اﷲِ وَ عَلیٰ \nBISMILLAAHE WA BILLAAHE WA FEE SABEELILLAAHE WA A’LAA\nIn the name of Allah and by Allah and in the way of Allah and on the \nمِلَّۃِ رَسُوْلِ اﷲِ اَللّٰھُمَّ اَنَزِلْنِیْ مُنْزَلًا \nMILLATE RASOOLILLAAHE ALLAAHUMMA ANZILNEE MUNZALAN\nnation of the Apostle of Allah. O Allah, You send down upon me a blessed \nمُبَارَكًا وَ اَنْتَ خَیْرُ الْمُنْزِلِیْنَ\nMOBAARAKAN WA ANTA KHAYRUL MUNZELEENA\nstation and You are the best of those who reveal. \nYou may then say the following words:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ كَبِیْرًا وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ كَثِیْرًا وَ سُبْحَانَ \nALLAAHO AKBARO KABEERAN WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE KASEERAN WA SUBHAANAL\nAllah is most great and abundant praise is for Allah and I glorify Allah \nاﷲِ بُكْرَۃً وَ اَصِیْلًا وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الْفَرْدِ \nLAAHE BUKRATAN WA ASEELAN WAL HAMDOLILLAAHIL FARDIS\nmorning and evening. All Praise belongs to Allah, the Unique, \nالصَّمَدِ الْمَاجِدِ الْاَحَدِ الْمُتَفَضِّلِ الْمَنَّانِ \nSAMADIL MAAJEDIL AHADIL MOTAFAZZELIL MANNAANIL\nthe Self-Sufficient, the Majestic, the One, the Gracious, the Obliger, the Benevolent, \nالْمُتَطَوِّلِ الْحَنَّانِ الَّذِیْ مِنْ تَطَوُّلِهٖ سَهَّلَ \nMOTA-TAWWELIL HANNAANIL LAZEE MIN TA-TAWWOLEHI SAH-HALA\nthe Benefactor, the One due to whose Benevolence and Goodness. He has eased \nلِیْ زِیَارَۃَ مَوْلَایَ بِاِحْسَانِهٖ وَلَمْ یَجْعَلْنِیْ \nLEE ZEYAARATA MAWLAAYA BE EHSAANEHI WA LAM YAJ-A’LNEE \nfor me the visitation of my visitation and did not prevent me from \nعَنْ زِیَارَتِهٖ مَمْنُوْعًا وَلَا عَنْ ذِمَّتِهٖ مَدْفُوْعًا \nA’N ZEYAARATEHI MAMNOO-A’N WA LAA A’N ZIMMATEHI MAD-FOO-A’N\nit and has not stopped me from the discharge of my responsibilities. \nبَلْ تَطَوَّلَ وَ مَنَحَ\nBAL TATAWWALA WA MANAHA\nRather He has favoured and honoured me.\nYou may then enter the shrine. When you reach its center, you may stop near the tomb with reverence, weeping, and submission, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَارِثَ اٰدَمَ صَفْوَۃِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA AADAMA SAFWATIL LAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Adam the sincerely attached friend of Allah!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَاوَارِثَ نُوْحٍ اَمِیْنِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA NOOHIN AMEENIL LAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Nooh, the prophet of Allah!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَارِثَ اِبْرَاهِیْمَ خَلِیْلِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELIL LAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Abraham, the intimate friend of Allah!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَارِثَ مُوْسیٰ كَلِیْمِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA MOOSAA KALEEMIL LAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Moses who spoke to Allah!\nاَلسَّلامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَارِثَ عِیْسیٰ رُوْحِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA E’ESAA ROOHIL LAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Jesus who received peace, joy, and mercy from Allah!\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّی \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA MOHAMMADIN SALLAL\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Mohammad, blessings of\nاﷲُ عَلَیْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ حَبِیْبِ اﷲِ \nLAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI HABEEBILLAAHE\nAllah be upon him and his family, the dearest beloved of Allah!\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَارِثَ عَلِیٍّ حُجَّۃٍ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WAARESA A’LIYYIN HUJJATILLAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the inheritor of Amir ul-Mu’minin, peace be upon him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ اَیُّهَا الْوَصِیُّ الْبَرُّ التَّقِیُّ \nASSAALAMO A’LAYKA AYYOHAL WASIYYUL BARRUT TAQIYYO\nPeace be on you, O the vicegerent, the righteous, the pious\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا ثَارَاﷲِ وَابْنَ ثَارِهٖ وَالْوِتْرَ الْمَوْتُوْرَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SAARALLAAHE WABNA SAAREHI WAL WITRAL MAWTOORA\nPeace be on you, O he whose blood-claimer is Allah, He is the blood-claimer of your father also, as those who persecuted you, your relatives and friends have not been punished for the crimes.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلوٰۃَ وَ اٰتَیْتَ \nASH-HADO ANNAKA QAD AQAMTAS SALAATA WA AATAYTAZ\nI bear witness that verily you established the prayers, gave \nالزَّكوٰۃَ وَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَ نَهَیْتَ \nZAKAATA WA AMARTA BIL MA’ROOFE WA NAHAYTA\nthe zakat (prescribed share) to the needy, commanded to do what is right and lawful, not to do that \nعَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَ جَاهَدْتَ فِی اﷲِ حَقَّ \nA’NIL MUNKARE WA JAAHADTA FILLAAHE HAQQA\nwhich is wrong and unlawful, and you fought in the way of Allah in letter and \nجِهَادِهِ حَتَّی اسْتُبِیْحَ حَرَمُكَ وَ قُتِلْتَ مَظْلُوْمًا\nJEHAADEHI HATTAS TOBEE-HA HARAMOKA WA QOTILTA MAZLOOMAN\nspirit till your sanctuary was violated and you were killed oppressively.\nYou may then stop at the side of the Imam’s head with submissive heart and teary eyes and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا اَبَا عَبْدِاﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA ABAA A’BDILLAAHE \nPeace be on you, O Abu Abdullah\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA RASOOLILLAAHE \nPeace be on you, O the son of the Apostle of Allah\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا بْنَ سَیِّدِ الْوَصِیِّیْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA SAYYEDILWASIYYEENA \nPeace be on you, O the son of the chief of the successors\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ فَاطِمَۃَ الزَّهْرَآئِ سَیِّدَۃِ نِسَآئِ الْعَالَمِیْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA FAATEMATAZ ZAHRAAA-E SAYYEDATE NESAAA-IL A’ALAMEENA \nPeace be on you, O the son of Fatemah Zahra, the chief of the women of the universe\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا بَطَلَ الْمُسْلِمِیْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA BATALAL MUSLEMEENA\nPeace be on you, O the valiant warrior of the Muslims.\nیَا مَوْلَایَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ كُنْتَ نُوْراً فِیْ \nYAA MAWLAAYA ASH-HADO ANNAKA KUNTA NOORAN FIL\nO my Master, I bear witness that verily you were a light in the \nالْاَصْلَابِ الشَّامِخَۃِ وَالْاَرْحَامِ الْمُطَهَّرَۃِ \nASLAABISH-SHAAMEKHATE WAL ARHAAMIL MOTAHHARATE\nsublime loins and purified wombs, \nلَمْ تُنَجِّسْكَ الْجَاهِلِیَّۃُ بِاَنْجَاسِهَا وَلَمْ \nLAM TONAJJISKAL JAAHELIYYATO BE ANJAASEHAA WA LAM\nthe impurities of ignorance did not even touch you, nor \nتُلْبِسْكَ مِنْ مُدْ لَهِمَّاتِ ثِیَابِهَا \nTULBISKA MIN MUDLAHIMMAATE SEYAABEHAA\ncould its soiled and dirty bearing ever smear you.\nوَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ مِنْ دَعَآئِمِ الدِّیْنِ وَ اَرْكَانِ \nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKA MIN  DA-AAA-EMID DEENE WA ARKAANIL\nI bear witness that, verily, you are the mainstay of the religion, and the support\nالْمُسْلِمِیْنَ وَ مَعْقِلِ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ \nMUSLEMEENA WA MA’QELIL MOMENEENA\nof the Muslims and the sanctuary of the believers. \nوَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ الْاِمَامُ الْبَرُّالتَّقِیُّ الرَّضِیُّ \nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKAL EMAAMUL BARRUT TAQIYYUR RAZIYYUZ\nI bear witness that, verily, you are a righteous, pious, satisfied,\nالزَّكِیُّ الْهَادِیْ الْمَهْدِیّ وَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّ \nZAKIYYUL HAADIL MAHDIYYE WA ASH-HADO ANNAL\nchaste, guide, guided, and I bear witness that\nالْاَئِمَّۃَ مِنْ وُلْدِكَ كَلِمَۃُ التّقْویٰ وَاَعْلَامُ \nA-IMMATA MIN WULDEKA KALAMATUT TAQWAA WA A-ALAAMUL\nthe leaders from your progeny are the words of piety and the standards \nالْهُدیٰ وَالْعُرْوَۃُ الْوُثْقٰی وَالْحُجَّۃُ عَلٰی\nHODAA WAL U’RWATUL WUSQAA WAL HUJJATO A’LAA\nof guidance and the strong rope and proofs upon\nاَهْلِ الدُّنْیَا\nAHLID DUNYAA\nthe people of the world.\nYou may then throw yourself on the tomb and say the following words:\nاِنَّا لِلّٰهِ وَ اِنَّا اِلَیْهِ رَاجِعُوْنَ یَامَوْلَایَ اَنَا \nINNAA LILLAAHE WA INNAA ELAYHE RAA-JE-O’ONA YAA MAWLAAYA ANAA\nTo Allah do we belong and unto Him shall we return. O my master, I am \nمُوَالٍ لِوَلِیِّكُمْ وَ مُعَادٍ لِعَدُوِّكُمْ وَ اَنَا بِكُمْ \nMOWAALIN LE WALIYYEKUM WA MO-A’ADIN LE A’DUWWEKUM WA ANAA BEKUM\na friend of your friends and an enemy to your enemy. I believe in you \nمُؤْمِنٌ وَ بِاِیَاكُمْ مُوْقِنٌ بِشَرَایِعِ دِیْنِیْ وَ \nMOA-MENUN WA BE EYAAKUM MOOQENUN BE SHA-RAA-YE-E’ DEENEE WA\nand am certain about your return along with the laws of my religion and \nخَوَاتِیْمِ عَمَلِیْ وَ قَلْبِیْ لِقَلْبِكُمْ سِلْمٌ وَ \nKHAWAATEEME A’MALEE WA QALBEE LE QALBEKUM SILMUN WA\nthe end result of my deeds and my heart submits to your heart and \nاَمْرِیْ لِأَمْرِكُمْ مُتَّبِعٌ یَا مَوْلَایَ اَتَیْتُكَ \nAMREE LE AMREKUM MUTTABE-O’ON YAA MAWLAAYA ATAYTOKA\nmy affair follows your command. O my master! I come to you \nخَائِفًا فَاٰمِنِّیْ وَ اَتَیْتُكَ مُسْتَجِیْراً فَاَجِرْنِیْ \nKHAA-EFAN FA-AAMINNEE WA ATAYTOKA MUSTAJEERAN FA-AJIRNEE\nas a fearful person then grant me security and I come to you as one seeking your refuge then grant me cover \nوَ اَتَیْتُكَ فَقِیْراً فَاَغْنِنِیْ سَیِّدِیْ وَ مَوْلَایَ \nWA ATYATOKA FAQEERAN FA-AGHNENEE SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA\nand I come to you as a destitute. Then you make me needless of other. O my master and my chief, \nاَنْتَ مَوْلَایَ حُجَّۃُ اﷲِ عَلَی الْخَلْقِ \nANTA MAWLAAYA HUJJATULLAAHE A’LAL KHALQE\nyou are my master, the proof of Allah upon the entire \nاَجْمَعِیْنَ اٰمَنْتَُ بِسِرِّكُمْ وَ عَلَانِیَّتِكُمْ وَ \nAJ-MAE’ENA AAMANTO BE SIRREKUM WA A’LAANIYYATEKUM WA\ncreation. I believe in your hidden and your evident affairs and \nبِظَاهِرِكُمْ وَ بَاطِنِكُمْ وَ اَوّلِكُمْ وَ اٰخِرُكُمْ \nBE JAAHEREKUM WA BAATENEKUM WA AWWALEKUM WA AAKHEREKUM\nyour exterior and your interior and your first and your last. \nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ التَّالِیْ لِكِتابِ اﷲِ وَ اَمِیْنُ \nWA ASH-HADO ANNAKAT TAALEE LE-KETAABILLAAHE WA AMEENUL\nAnd I bear witness that you are the reciter the Book of Allah and the trustee \nاﷲِ الدَّاعِی اِلَی اﷲِ بِالحْكْمَۃِ وَالْمَوْعِظَۃِ \nLAAHID DAA-E’EE ELALLAAHE BIL HIKMATE WAL MAW-E’ZATIL \nof Allah and the caller towards Allah with wisdom and goodly \nالْحَسَنَۃِ لَعَنَ اﷲُ اُمَّۃً ظَلَمَتْكَ وَ اُمَّۃً \nHASANATE LA-A’NALLAAHO UMMATAN ZALAMATKA WA UMMATAN\nadmonition. May Allah curse the people who have oppressed you and the people who have \nقَتَلَتْكَ وَ لَعَنَ اﷲُ اُمَّۃً سَمِعَتْ بِذَالِكَ \nQATALATKA WA LA-A’NALLAAHO UMMATAN SAME-A’T BE ZAALEKA\nkilled you and the people who heard about it \nفَرَضِیَتْ بِهٖ\nFA-RAZEYAT BEHI\nbut agree to it.\nYou may then offer a two-unit prayer to the side of the Imam’s head and when you finish, you may say the following words:\nاَللّٰھُمَّ اِنِّیْ لَكَ صَلَّیْتُ وَ لَكَ رَكَعْتُ وَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE LAKA SALLAAYTO WA LAKA RA-KA’TO WA\nO Allah! I have prayed to You\nلَكَ سَجَدْتُ وَ حَدْكَ لَا شَرِیْكَ لَكَ فَاِنَّهٗ\nLAKA SAJADTO WAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAKA FA INNAHU\nand I have bowed down before You and I prostrate in front of You. You are One, There is no partner unto You \nلَا تَجُوْزُ الصَّلوٰۃُ وَالرُّكُوعُ وَالسُّجُوْدُ \nLAA TAJOOZUS SALAATO WAR ROKOO-O’ WAS SOJOODO\nas there is no prayer or bowing or prostration except for You. \nاِلاَّ لَكَ لِاَنَّكَ اَنْتَ اﷲُ الَّذِیْ لَا اِلٰهَ اَنْتَ \nILLAA LAKA LE ANNAKA ANTALLAAHUL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ANTA\nFor surely You are Allah. There is no God except You. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلیٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ \nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN WA\nO Allah! Send blessings on Mohammad and the progeny of Mohammad and \nاَبْلِغْهُمْ عَنِّیْ اَفْضَلَ السَّلَامِ وَالتَّحِیَّۃِ \nABLIGH-HUM A’NNEE AFZALAS SALAAME WAT TAHIYYATE\nmake the best form of greetings and salutations reach them from my side. And also send back to me their greetings and salutations.\nوَارْدُدْ عَلَيَّ مِنْهُمُ السَّلَامَ \nWAR-DUD A’LAYYA MINHOMUS SALAAMA \nmake the best form of greetings and salutations reach them from my side. And also send back to me their greetings and salutations.\nاللّٰهُمَّ وَ هَاتَانِِ الرَّكْعَتَانِ هَدِیَّۃٌ مِنِّیْ اِلیٰ \nALLAAHUMMA WA HAATAANIR RAK-A’TAANE HADIYYATUN MINNEE ELAA \nO Allah! These are two cycles of prayers, which is a gift from my side in the service \nسَیِّدِیْ الْحُسَیْنِ بنِ عَلِیٍّ عَلَیْهِمَا السَّلَامُ \nSAYYEDIL HUSAYNIBNE A’LIYYIN A’LAYHEMAS SALAAMO \nof my master and leader and my chief Husayn ibn Ali, peace be upon both of them.\nاَللّٰھُمَّ صَلِّ عَلیٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ عَلَیْهِ وَ \nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA A’LAYHE WA \nO Allah! Send blessings on Mohammad and the progeny of Mohammad and\nتَقَبَّلْهُمَا مِنّیْ وَاجْزِنِیْ عَلَیْهِمَا اَفْضَلَ \nTAQABBAL-HOMAA MINNEE WAJ-ZENEE A’LAYHEMAA AFZALA \nand accept that from me and reward me for that to the extent \nاَمَلِیْ وَ رَجَآئِیْ فِیْكَ وَ فِیْ وَلِیِّكَ یَا وَلِیَّ \nAMALEE WA RA-JAAA-EE FEEKA WA FEE WALIYYEKA YAA WALIYYAL \nof my greatest desires and hopes from You and Your representative\nالْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ\nMOMINEENA.\nof the believers\nYou may then throw yourself on the tomb, kiss it, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَی الْحُسَیْنِ بْنِ عَلِیٍّ الْمَظْلُوْمِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAL HUSAYNIBNE A’LIYYENIL MAZLOOMISH\nPeace be on Husayn son of Ali, the oppressed, \nالشَّهِیْدِ قَتِیْلِ الْعَبْرَاتِ وَ اَسِیْرِ الْكُرُبَاتِ \nSHAHEEDE QATEELIL A’BRAATE WA ASEERIL KOROBAATE\nthe martyred, the one who was killed while he was in tears and the one engulfed in calamities.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّیْ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّهٗ وَلِیُّكَ وَابْنُ وَلِیِّكَ وَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ASH-HADO ANNAHU WALIYYOKA WABNO WALIYYEKA WA\nO Allah, I bear witness that he is Your representative and the son of Your representative and \nصَفِیُّكَ الثَّائِرُ بِحَقِّكَ اَكْرَمْتَهُ بِكَرَامَتِكَ \nSAFIYYOKAS SAA-ERO BE HAKKEKA AKRAMTAHU BE KARAAMATEKA \nYour chosen one, the one who will take revenge by Your right, You have honoured him by Your nobility \nوَ خَتَمْتَ لَهٗ بِالشَّهَادَۃِ وَ جَعَلْتَهٗ سَیِّدًا مِنَ \nWA KHATAMTA LAHU BISH SHA-HAADATE WA JA-A’LTAHU SAYYEDAN MENAS \nand have sealed his fate with martyrdom and have made him as a leader \nالسَّادَۃِ وَ قَائِدًا مِنَ الْقَادَۃِ وَ اَكْرَمْتَهٗ\nSAADATE WA QAAEDAN MENAL QAADATE WA AKRAMTAHU\nof the leaders and a guide of the guides and You have honoured him \nبِطِیْبِ الْوِلَادَۃِ وَاعْظَمْتَه مَوَارِیْثَ الْاَنْبِیَائِ \nBE TEEBIL WELAADATE WA’ZAMTAHU MAWAAREESAL ANBEYAA-E\nwith a pure lineage and granted him the inheritance of the Prophets \nوَ جَعَلْتَهٗ حُجَّۃً عَلیٰ خَلْقِكَ مِنَ \nWA JA-A’LTAHU HUJJATAN A’LAA KHALQEKA MENAL \nand made him a proof over Your creation\nالْاَوْصِیَآئِ فَاَعْذَرَ فِیْ الدُّعَآئِ و َمَنَحَ \nAWSEYAAA-E FA-AA’ZARA FID DO-AAA-E WA MANAHAN\nfrom the vicegerents. Then he fulfilled the right of calling (towards You) and offered \nالنَّصِیْحَۃَ وَ بَذَلَ مُهْجَتَهٗ فِیْكَ حَتَّی \nNASEEHATA WA BAZALA MOH-JATAHU FEEKA HATTAS\nadvice and laid down his life for You \nاسْتَنْقَذَ عِبَادَكَ مِنَ الْجَهَالَۃِ وَ حَیْرَۃِ \nTANQAZA E’BAADAKA MENAL JAHAALATE WA HAYRATIZ\nto the extent that he removed Your servants from ignorance and the perplexity of \nالضَّلالَۃِ وَ قَدْ تَوَازَرَ عَلَیْهِ مَنْ غَرَّتْهُ \nZALAALATE WA QAD TAWAA-ZARA A’LAYHE MIN GHARRAT-HUD\ndeviation. Then a group rose up against him who had been deceived \nالدُّنْیَا وَ بَاعَ حَظَّهُ مِنَ الْاٰخِرَۃِ بِالْاَدْنیٰ وَ \nDUNYAA WA BAA-A’ HAZZAHU MENAL AAKHERATE BIL AD-NAA WA\nby this world and had sold their share of the hereafter for a measly remuneration and \nتَرَدیّٰ فِیْ هُوَاهُ وَ اَسْخَطَكَ وَ اَسْخَطَ \nTARADDAA FEE HOWAAHO WA AS-KHATAKA WA AS-KHATA\nperished in their carnal desires and angered You and \nنَبِیِّكَ وَ اَطَاعَ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ اُولِی الشِّقَاقِ \nNABIYYEKA WA A-TAA-A’ MIN E’BAADEKA OOLISH SHEQAAQE\nYour Prophet and obeyed from Your servants the people of discord, \nوَالنِّفَاقِ وَ حَمَلَۃَ الْاَوْزَارِ الْمُسْتَوْحِبِیْنَ \nWAN NEFAAQE WA HAMALATAL AWZAARIL MUSTAWHEBEENAN\nand hypocrisy and the committer of sins which makes them deserve \nالنَّارَ فَجَاهَدَهُمْ فِیْكَ صَابِراً مُحْتَسِباً \nNAARA FA JAAHADAHUM FEEKA SAABERAN MOHTASEBAN\nHell-fire. Then he fought against such people in Your way as a patient, expectant, \nمُقْبِلًا غَیْرَ مُدْبِرٍ لَا تَاْخُذُهٗ فِیْ اﷲِ لَوْمَۃُ \nMUQBELAN GHAYRA MUDBERAN LAA TA-KHOZOHU FILLAAHE LAWMATO\nstepping forward and not turning back. The slandering of any maligner did not affect him in the \nلآئِمٍ حَتّٰی سُفِكَ فِیْ طَاعَتِكَ دَمُهٗ\nLAAA-EMIN HATTAA SOFEKA FEE TAA-A’TEKA DAMOHU\nway of Allah till his blood was shed in Your way and \nوَاسْتُبِیْحَ حَرِیْمُهُ اَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْهُمْ لَعْنًا وَبِیْلًا \nWAS TOBEEHA HAREEMOHU ALLAAHUMMAL A’NHUM LA’NAN  WABEELAN\nhis sanctity was violated. O Allah! Curse them with a calamitous curse \nوَ عَذِّبْهُمْ عَذَاباً اَلِیْمًا \nWA A’ZZIBHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAN\nand punish them with a painful punishment.\nYou may then turn to ‘Ali ibn al-Husayn (a.s.), who is buried to the side of Imam al-Husayn’s feet, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا وَلِیَّ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA WALIYYALLAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the representative of Allah.\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا بْنَ رَسُوْلِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA RASOOLILLAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the son of the Apostle of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ خَاتَمِ النَّبِیِّیْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA\nPeace be on you, O the son of the last of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ فَاطِمَۃَ سَیَّدَۃِ نِسَآئِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA FAATEMATA SAYYEDATE NESAAA-IL A’ALAMEENA\nPeace be on you, O the son of Fatemah, the leader of the women of the Universe.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَابْنَ اَمِیْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MOMINEENA\nPeace be on you, O the son of the commander of the faithful.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ اَیُّهَا الْمَظْلُوْمُ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA AYYOHAL MAZLOOMUSH\nPeace be on you, O the oppressed, \nالشَّهِیْدُ بِاَبِیْ اَنْتَ وَ اُمِّیْ عِشْتَ سِعِیْدًا \nSHAHEEDO BE ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE ISHTA SA-E’EDAN\nthe martyred May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you, \nوَ قُتِلْتَ مَظْلُوْماً شَهِیْدًا \nWA QOTILTA MAZLOOMAN SHAHEEDAN\nyou lived a very fortunate life and were killed as oppressed martyred.\nYou may then turn to the tombs of the martyrs - may Allah’s pleasure be upon them - and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ اَیُّهَا الذّٰابُونَ عَنْ تَوْحِیْدِ اﷲِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA AYYOHAZ ZAABBOONA A’N TAWHEEDILLAAHE\nPeace be on you, O the defenders of the unity of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكُمْ بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ فَنِعْمَ عَقْبَی \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM BEMAA SABARTUM FA NEA’MA AQBAD\nPeace be on you, for what you were patient upon, then you have the best \nالدَّارِ بِاَبِیْ اَنْتُمْ وَ اُمِّیْ فُزْتُمْ فَوْزاً عَظِیْمًا\nDAARE BE ABEE ANTUM WA UMMEE FUZTUM FAWZAN A’ZEEMAN\nabode in the hereafter. May my father and my mother be sacrificed for you, you have attained a great success.\nYou may then walk to the shrine of al-’Abbas ibn ‘Ali, stop at his holy tomb, and say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ اَیُّهَا الْعَبْدُ الصَّالِحُ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA AYYOHAL A’BDUS SAALEHO\nPeace be on you, O the righteous servant \nوَالصِّدِّیْقُ الْمُوَاسِیْ \nWAS SIDDEEQUL MOWAASEE \nand truthful who is beneficial. \nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ اَمَنْتَ بِاﷲِ وَ نَصَرْتَ ابْنَ \nASH-HADO ANNAKA AMANTA BILLAAHE WA NASARTABNA \nI bear witness that you believed in Allah and helped the son of \nرَسُوْلِ اﷲِ وَ دَعَوْتَ اِلیٰ سَبِیْلِ اﷲِ وَ \nRASOOLILLAAHE WA DA-A’WTA ELAA SABEELILLAAHE WA \nthe Apostle of Allah and you called towards the way of Allah and \nوَاسَیْتَ بِنَفْسِكَ عَلَیْكَ مِنَ اﷲِ اَفْضَلُ التَّحِیَّۃِ وَالسَّلَامِ \nWAA SAYTA BE NAFSEKA A’LAYKA MENALLAAHE AFZALUT TAHIYYATE WASSALAAME \nlaid down your own  life, then upon you be the best of greetings and salutation from Allah.\nYou may now throw yourself on the tomb and say the following words:\nبِاَبِیْ اَنْتَ وَ اَمِّیْ یَا نَاصِرَ دِیْنِ اﷲِ  \nBE ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE YAA NAASERA DEENILLAAHE \nMay my father and my mother be sacrificed for you, O the helper of the religion of Allah. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَانَاصِرَ الْحُسِیْنِ الصِّدِّیْقِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA NAASERAL HUSAYNISH SIDDEEQE\nPeace be on you, O the helper of Husayn, the truthful. \nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا نَاصِرَ الْحُسَیْنِ الشَّهِیْدِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA NAASERAL HUSAYNISH SHAHEEDE\nPeace be on you, O the helper of Husayn, the martyr.\nعَلَیْكَ مِنِّیْ السَّلَامُ مَا بَقِیْتُ وَ بَقِیَ اللَّیْلُ \nA’LAYKA MINNIS SALAAMO MAA BAQEETO WA BAQEYAL LAYLO\nPeace be on you from me till the time I exist and the night and the \nوَالنَّهَارُ\nWAN NAHAARO\nday exist.\nYou may then stand up to offer a two-unit prayer to the side of his head and then repeat the same words that you have said after offering a prayer at Imam al-Husayn’s shrine. These words, which have been previously cited, begin with the following statement:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ‏ صَلَّيْتُ۔۔۔\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE SALLAYTO….\nO Allah! I prayed namaz….\nYou may then return to the shrine of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) to reside there for any period you like. However, it is recommended not to appoint the holy shrine as one’s place of residence and spending the night there.\nIf you intend to leave and bid farewell to the Imam (a.s.), you may stop at the side of the head and say the following words while weeping:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا مَوْلَایَ سَلَامَ مُوَدِّعٍ لَا \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA SALAAMA MOWADDE-I’N LAA \nPeace be on you, O my Master! This is the farewell salutation of the departing visitor, \nقَالٍ وَلَا سَئِمٍ فَاِنْ اَنْصَرِفْ فَلَا عَنْ مَلَالَۃٍ \nQAALIN WA LAA SA-EMIN FA-IN ANSARIF FALAA A’N MALAA-LATIN\nneither due to lack of interest, nor on account of fatigue; and if I go back, it is not because of uneasiness; and \nوَ اِنْ اُقِمْ فَلَا عَنْ سُوْٓئِ ظَنٍّ بِمَا وَعَدَ اﷲُ \nWA IN OQIM FALAA A’N SOOO-E ZANNIN BEMAA WA-A’DALLAAHUS\nif I stay, it is not in view of the tempting persuasion which Allah has set forth for \nالصَّابِرِیْنَ یَا مَوْلَایَ لَا جَعَلَهُ اﷲُ اٰخِرَ \nSAABEREENA YAA MAWLAAYA LAA JA-A’LAHULLAAHO AAKHERAL\nthose who endure. O my Master, may Allah let not my this visit to you be the last one, \nالْعَهْدِ مِنِّیْ لِزِیَارَتِكَ وَ رَزَقَنِی الْعَوْدَ \nA’HDE MINNEE LE ZEYAARATEKA WA RAZAQANIL A’WDA\nbut enable me to come back here again and again, \nاِلَیْكَ وَالْمَقَامَ فِیْ حَرَمِكَ وَالْكَوْنَ فِیْ \nELAYKA WAL MAQAAMA FEE HARAMEKA WAL KAWNA FEE\nvisit your holy Haram and be near your resting \nمَشْهَدِكَ اٰمِیْنَ رَبَّ الْعَالَمِیْنَ\nMASH-HADEKA AAMEEN RABBAL A’ALAMEENA\nabode. So let it be, O Lord of the worlds! \nYou may then kiss the tomb and try to pass your entire body over it, because this tomb is security and protection. You may then leave it by walking backwards without giving your back to the tomb. You may say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا بَابَ الْمَقَامَ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA BAABAL MAQAAMA\nPeace be on you, O the door of dignity.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا شَرِیْكَ الْقُرْآنِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SHAREEKAL QUR-AAANE\nPeace be on you, O the associate of Holy Quran.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا حُجَّۃَ الْخِصَامِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA HUJJATAL KHESAAME\nPeace be on you, O the argument of Allah against the enemies.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ یَا سَفِیْنَۃَ النَّجَاۃِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA YAA SAFEENATAN NAJAATE\nPeace be on you, O the ark of salvation.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا مَلآئِكَۃَ رَبِّیْ الْمُقِیْمِیْنَ فِیْ هٰذَا الْحَرَمِ \nASSALAAMO A’LAYKUM YAA MALAAA-EKATA RABBIL MOQEEMEENA FEE HAAZAL HARAME\nPeace be on you, O the angles of my Lord who reside in this sanctuary.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَیْكَ اَبَدًا مَا بَقِیْتُ وَ بَقِیَ اللَّیْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ\nASSALAAMO A’LAYKA ABADAN MAA BAQEETO WA BAQEYAL LAYLO WAN NAHAARO\nPeace be on you always till I exist and the night and the day exist.\nYou may also say the following words:\nاِنَّا لِلّٰهِ وَ اِنَّا اِلَیْهِ رَاجِعُوْنَ وَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا \nINNAA LILLAAHE WA INNAA ELAYHE RAAJE-O’ONA WA LAA HAWLA \nTo Allah we belong to Him shall we return. And there is no Power \nقُوَّۃَ اِلاَّ بِاﷲِ الْعَلِیَّ الْعَظِیْمِ\nWA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEME\nno Strength except with Allah, the exalted, the great.\nYou may then leave.\nSayyid Ibn Tawus and Muhammad ibn al-Mashhadi said, “If you do all these devotional acts (correctly), you will be as if you have visited Almighty Allah in His Divine Throne.”",
  "merits": "According to a validly reported tradition on the authority of a valid chain of authority, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said, “Whoever visits the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) at one of the following three nights, will have all his sins forgiven by Almighty Allah, including the past and the coming: the night before ‘Id al-Fitr Day, the night before ‘Id al-Azha Day, and the mid-Sha’ban night.”According to another validly reported tradition, Imam Musa ibn Ja’far (al-Kazim) (a.s.) has said, “Whoever visits (Imam) al-Husayn (a.s.) at these three nights, will have all his sins forgiven by Almighty Allah, both the past and the coming: the mid-Sha’ban night, the twenty-third night of Ramazan, and the ‘Id al-Fitr night.”Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said, “If one visits al-Husayn ibn ‘Ali at the mid-Sha’ban night, the ‘Id al-Fitr night, and the ‘Arafat night in the same year, Almighty Allah will record for him the reward of one thousand times of admissible hajj and one thousand times of acceptable ‘umrah and will grant him one thousand requests for this world and the Hereafter.”Imam al-Baqir (a.s.) is reported to have said, “Whoever spends the ‘Arafat Night in the land of Karbala’ and resides to spend the ‘Arafat Day there and then leaves, Almighty Allah shall save him from the evils of that year.”"
}
